{"_id":"6a2ff52a2204ffbc59e5a5ea","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"nDUOJPCEzkCxX8B63HBP3","description":"# CSV\n\nCSV (Comma-Separated Values) is the most common format for tabular data exchange. `pd.read_csv()` loads a CSV file into a DataFrame and accepts dozens of parameters for handling separators, missing values, date parsing, and data types. CSV files are human-readable but lack type information, so columns often need type correction after loading.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"pandas.read_csv","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.read_csv.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb76"},{"type":"article","title":"Pandas Read CSV","url":"https://www.w3schools.com/python/pandas/pandas_csv.asp","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb77"},{"type":"video","title":"How to Read a CSV file into a Pandas DataFrame","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4YI9z1qUpew","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb78"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:50:50.330Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/nDUOJPCEzkCxX8B63HBP3.md"}